{
  "id": "find-all-numbers-disappeared-in-an-array",
  "questionId": "find-all-numbers-disappeared-in-an-array",
  "slug": "find-all-numbers-disappeared-in-an-array",
  "title": "Find All Numbers Disappeared in an Array",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Cyclic sort",
  "patterns": [
    "cyclic sort",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "every value v in [1, n] wants to sit at index v-1. what happens if you rearrange the array so every value is at its 'home' index, wherever possible?",
    "walk through the array, and while nums[i] isn't already at its home index and that home index doesn't already hold the correct value, swap it there",
    "duplicates mean two copies of the same value both want the same home index - only one can have it, so a slot with no correct owner stays 'wrong'",
    "after placement, scan the array: any index i where nums[i] != i+1 tells you that i+1 is one of the missing numbers"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using O(n) extra space with a hash set when the problem is intended to be solved with O(1) extra space via in-place placement",
    "infinite looping when swapping duplicate values that both want the same target index, because the swap condition doesn't check if the target already holds the correct value",
    "forgetting to convert between value and index (value v belongs at index v-1, not index v)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array `nums` of length `n` where every value is in the\nrange `[1, n]`. Some values appear twice and others don't appear at all.\n\n**Return a list of all the numbers in `[1, n]` that are missing from the array, in ascending order.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "array length is n, every value is in range [1, n]",
      "some values may appear twice, some may be missing entirely",
      "return missing numbers in ascending order"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "no numbers are missing (empty result)",
      "every number is duplicated except one, so almost the whole range is missing",
      "array of length 1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
